const tail = "Diagnosis recorded: the remaining input is not geometric.  Once the two-pullback statement\nis corrected to a *pullback* square (S1911) and the point is handled by 2-Yoneda, the whole\ninverse construction and `S1878EssSurj` follow formally.";
const addRaw = String.raw`

## S1968 — actual q_v q-pilot object; the paper strip is R6's exact first missing (2026-11-01)

File: @BT@tmp/sheaf/xif/paper/S1968QVDeterminedQPilotActual.lean@BT@ (compiles, EXIT=0;
axioms @BT@propext@BT@, @BT@Classical.choice@BT@, @BT@Quot.sound@BT@ only; SHA256 source
@BT@054904288F47BD6B8FECBE59D03F94641024E15199AC3A6F840A11A8D684547C@BT@, olean
@BT@01C75B14E8D7CED5AAD6C5CECF4B2F248A6943D5B9055F87F51C5B46EE6572B5@BT@).

Built (actual): the actual @BT@q_v@BT@ data of the S1527/S1895 input
(@BT@paperQV@BT@, nonzero/contracting/log-negative; actual completed-DVR order
@BT@paperQVOrder@BT@ = @BT@S1487Cand.order@BT@ = @BT@order_C3@BT@; hence
@BT@|log q_b| = order_b * log 5@BT@, and the q_v determines the order as
@BT@order_b = |log q_b| / log 5@BT@), and the q-pilot **object** of IUT III,
Def. 3.8(i), at the object level: @BT@paperQPilotDivisor D@BT@ is the order-weighted
zero-locus arithmetic divisor in S1927's global realified Frobenioid
@BT@C^boxplus_mod@BT@, with
@BT@deg = sum_b |log q_b| = order_C3 * log 5 > 0@BT@
(@BT@paperQPilotDivisor_deg_eq_source@BT@, @BT@paperQPilotDivisor_deg_pos@BT@) and
q-pilot log-volume
@BT@paperQPilotLogVolume D = -deg = sourceQPilotSignedLog = -localLogMagnitude S1487Cand
= -order_C3 * log 5 < 0@BT@ (@BT@paperQPilotLogVolume_eq_neg_deg@BT@, @BT@_neg@BT@).
@BT@QVDeterminedQPilotObject@BT@ packages divisor/degree/log-volume with these
equalities; it is inhabited for every @BT@S1895PaperInput@BT@.

Obstructions proved: (i) the reduced anchor is the S1487 shear strip
(@BT@reducedQPilotAnchor D = S1487Strip 1 0@BT@), whose value monoid is
@BT@SourceHaarActualValueMonoid = Multiplicative {x : Real // x <= 0}@BT@ and whose
unit group is **trivial** (x <= 0 and -x <= 0 force x = 0).  Hence
@BT@(reducedQPilotTimesMu D).timesMu v@BT@ is a subsingleton for every v
(@BT@reducedQPilotTimesMu_subsingleton@BT@), and every candidate @BT@P@BT@ with
@BT@Nonempty (QPilotAnchorIdentification D P)@BT@ has subsingleton times-mu fibers at
every v (@BT@r6Proper_forces_trivial_timesMu@BT@).  The reduced anchor's x-mu layer
is therefore vacuous in the current value/unit model.
(ii) the tree's Hodge-theater strips are q_v-blind: changing only the initial
theta data keeps @BT@I.fPrimeStripAt n m@BT@ definitionally fixed
(@BT@withInitial@BT@, @BT@fPrimeStripAt_withInitial@BT@); the witness is
@BT@S1487FaithfulInput@BT@ vs @BT@S1487TwoPlaceInput@BT@ (same (1,0) strip and
canonical lift, q-pilot log-volumes @BT@-L@BT@ vs @BT@-2L@BT@; @BT@candidate_blind@BT@,
@BT@qPilot_scalar_differs@BT@).  So the candidate
@BT@canonical (I.fPrimeStripAt 1 0)@BT@ (= @BT@qPilotFTimesMuPrimeStripAt10@BT@) cannot
be certified q_v-determined.

First missing (a **definition**, not a proposition): a paper-side
@BT@paperQPilotFTimesMuStrip D : SourceFTimesMuPrimeStrip PaperV@BT@ arising from
@BT@paperQPilotDivisor D@BT@ via the associated-pilot-object construction of IUT II,
Def. 4.9(viii), plus its identification with that divisor.  The tree contains no
functor from the global realified Frobenioid (or from an arithmetic divisor) to a
prime strip; the only constructor is @BT@SourceFTimesMuPrimeStrip.canonical@BT@.
R6 proper is **not** closed; no fake strip, arbitrary inhabitant or Prop slot was
used.  The R6 interface itself is re-exported as @BT@R6Proper@BT@ /
@BT@r6Proper_iff@BT@ (S1960's reduction) and @BT@r6Proper_of_equivalence@BT@ is the
last step a future definition has to feed.

Consequence for S1967: @BT@OUnits D v = ((lgpStrip D).Mon v)^@BT@ is a subsingleton,
so any nontrivial @BT@OUnitsMu@BT@ / x-mu Kummer construction on this strip is vacuous
unless the value monoid of the strip is changed.
`;
const add = addRaw.split("@BT@").join("`");
const r = await tools.edit({ file_path: "AUDIT_LEDGER.md", old_string: tail, new_string: tail + add });
console.log(JSON.stringify(r).slice(0, 300));
", "description": "Append S1968 entry to audit ledger"}

